    "project": "marionette-racket-port",
    "summary": "Prove Racket distribution, prepare a parity lab, and hand Lee a mechanically bootstrapped 48-hour language project before any substantive port begins.",
    "prompt": "sounds amazing, so you know what's next? using marionette to plan the delivery of this. We've decided the actual implementation is human gated but we can let AI bootstrap the racket project (give it a fresh directory to start with so we can test for parity against TS before imports are introduced), do the CI, compile the binaries for github releases, and then handle the migration work so the extensions and skills use it (do we still keep a TS package that wraps the bin?). So the first thing is to open a baseline PR with a marionette plan for all this and then work to the human gate.",
